# .env.example — outline only, no implementation yet.
#
# Per the blueprint: this is the ONLY env file that gets committed —
# placeholders only, real values live in a gitignored .env (locally) and
# in Vault (on the VM). List the variable NAMES that database.py,
# auth.py, and docker-compose.yml will end up reading, with placeholder
# values, e.g. shaped like:
#
#   POSTGRES_USER=changeme
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
#   POSTGRES_DB=changeme
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://changeme:changeme@postgres:5432/changeme
#   JWT_SECRET_KEY=changeme
#
# Worth keeping in sync: every variable name here should match exactly
# what database.py / auth.py / docker-compose.yml actually read — a
# typo'd name here is a silent bug later (the real .env just won't have
# the variable the code is looking for).
